{
  "section_id": "s10-sea-land-breeze",
  "text": "Distance from the Sea (Sea Breeze and Land Breeze). Oceans and seas influence the climate of coastal areas. Water heats up and cools down more slowly than land. During the day, land heats up faster than water, causing a sea breeze to blow from the sea to the land. At night, the land cools down quickly, and a land breeze blows from land to the sea. This keeps coastal areas cooler in summer and warmer in winter compared to inland regions.",
